    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:21/seg:0",
      "source": "With BFO providing an underlying structure, this ontology encompasses fundamental categories and principles, enabling better communication and synergistic understanding among professionals.",
      "source_hash": 9952324776887929971,
      "context_hash": 10155229924238988771,
      "translation": "BFO가 기반 구조를 제공하므로, 이 온톨로지는 근본적인 범주와 원리를 포괄하며 전문가들 사이에서 더 나은 소통과 시너지 있는 이해를 가능하게 합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:12.222255Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:22/seg:0",
      "source": "The hierarchical composition of BFO distinguishes major ontological categories, reflective of our comprehension of reality:",
      "source_hash": 17392232153624154205,
      "context_hash": 13300546871766110439,
      "translation": "BFO의 계층적 구성은 실재에 대한 우리의 이해를 반영하여 주요 온톨로지 범주를 구분합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:12.222255Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:23/seg:0",
      "source": "Entity",
      "source_hash": 10984063758637754107,
      "context_hash": 1942391540930896051,
      "translation": "개체(Entity)",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:12.222255Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:24/seg:0",
      "source": "As the overarching category in BFO, entities encompass every conceivable existence, which is bifurcated into:",
      "source_hash": 8522167006697331433,
      "context_hash": 13380683034670869220,
      "translation": "BFO의 최상위 범주인 개체는 상상할 수 있는 모든 존재를 포괄하며, 다음과 같이 두 갈래로 나뉩니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:12.222255Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:25/seg:0",
      "source": "**Continuants**: Entities retaining their identity across time, including:",
      "source_hash": 11859558507320514509,
      "context_hash": 4979504700311538264,
      "translation": "**연속체(Continuants)**: 시간이 흘러도 자신의 동일성을 유지하는 개체로, 다음을 포함합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "Continuants": "Continuant"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:12.222256Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:26/seg:0",
      "source": "**Material Entities**: Tangible objects like cells and tissues.",
      "source_hash": 1431790949836237589,
      "context_hash": 8674033797889209434,
      "translation": "**물질적 개체(Material Entities)**: 세포나 조직과 같은 유형의 객체입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:12.222256Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:27/seg:0",
      "source": "**Immaterial Entities**: Non-physical elements like policies or ideas.",
      "source_hash": 4223546728346269912,
      "context_hash": 13414625129748782793,
      "translation": "**비물질적 개체(Immaterial Entities)**: 정책이나 아이디어와 같은 비물리적 요소입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:12.222256Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:28/seg:0",
      "source": "**Occurrents**: Time-bound occurrences, for example, biological processes like cell division.",
      "source_hash": 4199602655361406174,
      "context_hash": 10008843456074407467,
      "translation": "**발생체(Occurrents)**: 시간에 묶인 사건으로, 예를 들어 세포 분열과 같은 생물학적 과정이 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:12.222256Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:29/seg:0",
      "source": "Dependent Continuants",
      "source_hash": 15716182746519447481,
      "context_hash": 8254240724987973728,
      "translation": "의존 연속체(Dependent Continuants)",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "Continuants": "Continuant"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:12.222256Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:30/seg:0",
      "source": "These entities necessitate the existence of others for their survival, incapable of standalone presence.",
      "source_hash": 8576025797002161530,
      "context_hash": 453741254968525802,
      "translation": "이러한 개체는 존속하기 위해 다른 개체의 존재를 필요로 하며, 단독으로는 존재할 수 없습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582162Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:30/seg:1",
      "source": "They are differentiated into:",
      "source_hash": 940826044210107974,
      "context_hash": 6035364566051747991,
      "translation": "이들은 다음과 같이 구분됩니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582162Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:31/seg:0",
      "source": "**Specifically Dependent Continuant (SC)**: Qualities tethered to a singular entity, such as a car's color.",
      "source_hash": 5048622772266766935,
      "context_hash": 1283617994816305904,
      "translation": "**특정 의존 연속체(Specifically Dependent Continuant, SC)**: 자동차의 색처럼 단일 개체에 매여 있는 성질입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "Continuant": "Continuant"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582162Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:32/seg:0",
      "source": "**Generically Dependent Continuant (GC)**: Traits applicable across several instances, like the shared feature of \"redness\" in all red objects.",
      "source_hash": 7316605804872708436,
      "context_hash": 10326202872199253380,
      "translation": "**일반 의존 연속체(Generically Dependent Continuant, GC)**: 모든 빨간 물체가 공유하는 \"빨강\"이라는 특징처럼 여러 인스턴스에 걸쳐 적용될 수 있는 특성입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "Continuant": "Continuant"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582163Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:33/seg:0",
      "source": "Independent Continuants",
      "source_hash": 15054420640428442977,
      "context_hash": 971335467938382409,
      "translation": "독립 Continuant",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "Continuants": "Continuant"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:44:10.504528Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:34/seg:0",
      "source": "Entities within this category can exist autonomously, which includes:",
      "source_hash": 2245694573305689426,
      "context_hash": 11255566202461990307,
      "translation": "이 범주에 속하는 개체는 자율적으로 존재할 수 있으며, 다음을 포함합니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582163Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:35/seg:0",
      "source": "**Objects**: Individual material items, like a particular book.",
      "source_hash": 3847020752779242432,
      "context_hash": 826967224191615310,
      "translation": "**객체(Objects)**: 특정한 책 한 권처럼 개별적인 물질적 대상입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582163Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:36/seg:0",
      "source": "**Object Aggregates**: Assemblages of objects, such as a book collection.",
      "source_hash": 8259477457032274332,
      "context_hash": 9866613580711506875,
      "translation": "**객체 집합체(Object Aggregates)**: 책 컬렉션처럼 객체들이 모인 것입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582163Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:37/seg:0",
      "source": "**Fiat Objects**: Definitions based more on relational contexts than on innate physical characteristics, such as a designated parking space.",
      "source_hash": 16906301142398614317,
      "context_hash": 8614320299722486909,
      "translation": "**피아트 객체(Fiat Objects)**: 지정된 주차 공간처럼 고유한 물리적 특성보다는 관계적 맥락에 기반하여 정의되는 것입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582164Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:38/seg:0",
      "source": "Qualities",
      "source_hash": 4873665539410031754,
      "context_hash": 824030385736287529,
      "translation": "성질",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582164Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:39/seg:0",
      "source": "Observable or quantifiable characteristics of entities fall into this category, with illustrations like:",
      "source_hash": 9023005528213841507,
      "context_hash": 9065846503052184304,
      "translation": "개체의 관찰 가능하거나 정량화할 수 있는 특성이 이 범주에 속하며, 다음과 같은 예가 있습니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582164Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:40/seg:0",
      "source": "**Disposition**: A latent tendency to manifest a condition under specific circumstances, such as fragility.",
      "source_hash": 10398260784610104893,
      "context_hash": 1658667023782698556,
      "translation": "**성향(Disposition)**: 깨지기 쉬움처럼 특정한 상황에서 어떤 상태를 드러내는 잠재적 경향입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582164Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:41/seg:0",
      "source": "**Relational Quality**: Attributes elucidating relationships among entities, like a parental connection.",
      "source_hash": 13890822243525735644,
      "context_hash": 2495611368236888590,
      "translation": "**관계적 성질(Relational Quality)**: 부모 관계처럼 개체들 사이의 관계를 설명하는 속성입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582164Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:42/seg:0",
      "source": "Process",
      "source_hash": 14029994572002905463,
      "context_hash": 11820209017349083926,
      "translation": "과정",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582164Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:43/seg:0",
      "source": "Processes embody temporal developments or changes, which are definable through their involved entities and chronology.",
      "source_hash": 18288352301432637079,
      "context_hash": 18167084700432613913,
      "translation": "과정은 시간에 따른 전개나 변화를 구현하며, 관련된 개체와 시간 순서를 통해 정의할 수 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582164Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:43/seg:1",
      "source": "Key sub-categories include:",
      "source_hash": 1448110663573565949,
      "context_hash": 13964683193222392145,
      "translation": "주요 하위 범주는 다음과 같습니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582165Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:44/seg:0",
      "source": "**Process Boundary**: Markers denoting the commencement or termination of processes.",
      "source_hash": 4900681561119236521,
      "context_hash": 3938489524008945528,
      "translation": "**과정 경계(Process Boundary)**: 과정의 시작이나 종료를 나타내는 표지입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582165Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:45/seg:0",
      "source": "**History**: Documented sequences of events across a temporal expanse.",
      "source_hash": 15754411554010594720,
      "context_hash": 12757080097989222896,
      "translation": "**이력(History)**: 일정한 시간 범위에 걸쳐 기록된 사건의 연속입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582165Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:46/seg:0",
      "source": "Regions",
      "source_hash": 17930799848881899069,
      "context_hash": 12305614975012623764,
      "translation": "영역",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582165Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:47/seg:0",
      "source": "Regions cater to the demarcation of spatial or temporal planes where entities reside or events transpire:",
      "source_hash": 1049902784583934172,
      "context_hash": 8944688387849048747,
      "translation": "영역은 개체가 존재하거나 사건이 일어나는 공간적 또는 시간적 평면을 구획하는 역할을 합니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582165Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:48/seg:0",
      "source": "**Spatial Regions**: Three-dimensional spaces occupied by material entities.",
      "source_hash": 4927588845827547002,
      "context_hash": 700592499205260794,
      "translation": "**공간 영역(Spatial Regions)**: 물질적 개체가 차지하는 3차원 공간입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582165Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:49/seg:0",
      "source": "**Temporal Regions**: Linear time segments encompassing occurrences.",
      "source_hash": 5441522450449459601,
      "context_hash": 14277580660136578541,
      "translation": "**시간 영역(Temporal Regions)**: 사건을 포괄하는 선형적인 시간 구간입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "linear": "선형"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582165Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:50/seg:0",
      "source": "Extensions to BFO",
      "source_hash": 18072955272216580881,
      "context_hash": 3657665214427160930,
      "translation": "BFO의 확장",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582165Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:51/seg:0",
      "source": "To augment BFO's core ontology, **metaclasses**, which classify other classes, can be incorporated.",
      "source_hash": 4442010212358645594,
      "context_hash": 16180126089258295704,
      "translation": "BFO의 Core 온톨로지를 보강하기 위해 다른 클래스를 분류하는 **메타클래스**를 도입할 수 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "Core": "Core"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582165Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:51/seg:1",
      "source": "Additionally, the introduction of **variable-order classes**—abstract constructs designating classes whose exemplars may span various class orders or even include non-classes—is noteworthy.",
      "source_hash": 1045703124890391947,
      "context_hash": 7664711329779790433,
      "translation": "또한 **가변 차수 클래스(variable-order classes)**의 도입도 주목할 만합니다. 이는 그 사례가 여러 클래스 차수에 걸치거나 심지어 클래스가 아닌 것까지 포함할 수 있는 클래스를 지칭하는 추상적 구성물입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582166Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:51/seg:2",
      "source": "Unique to variable-order classes is their classification as a subclass and superclass of themselves.",
      "source_hash": 15054095331755096658,
      "context_hash": 5360742788400485693,
      "translation": "가변 차수 클래스만의 고유한 특징은 자기 자신의 서브클래스이자 슈퍼클래스로 분류된다는 점입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582166Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:52/seg:0",
      "source": "For example, the hierarchy of a \"Barack Obama\" is:",
      "source_hash": 16207424749146102724,
      "context_hash": 14849679609505890170,
      "translation": "예를 들어, \"Barack Obama\"의 계층 구조는 다음과 같습니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582166Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:53/seg:0",
      "source": "**Lower Ontology**",
      "source_hash": 15894308499106465895,
      "context_hash": 5267672251146851820,
      "translation": "**로어링하다 온톨로지(Lower Ontology)**",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "lower": "로어링하다"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582166Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:54/seg:0",
      "source": "\"Barack Obama\" instance of \"human\"",
      "source_hash": 12786656227328227222,
      "context_hash": 5428723873210859700,
      "translation": "\"Barack Obama\"는 \"human\"의 인스턴스",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582167Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:55/seg:0",
      "source": "\"human\" subclass of \"person\"",
      "source_hash": 10212846390774737217,
      "context_hash": 768037972081592053,
      "translation": "\"human\"은 \"person\"의 서브클래스",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582167Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:56/seg:0",
      "source": "\"person\" subclass of \"individual\"",
      "source_hash": 12619774205495153311,
      "context_hash": 14371541705936589964,
      "translation": "\"person\"은 \"individual\"의 서브클래스",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582167Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:57/seg:0",
      "source": "\"individual\" subclass of \"agent\"",
      "source_hash": 12201008961830479592,
      "context_hash": 6481678204666640503,
      "translation": "\"individual\"은 \"agent\"의 서브클래스",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:31:05.582167Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:58/seg:0",
      "source": "**Upper Ontology**",
      "source_hash": 10838193090399793537,
      "context_hash": 16835918733043795562,
      "translation": "**상위 온톨로지**",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:29:10.798094Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:59/seg:0",
      "source": "\"agent\" subclass of \"independent continuant\"",
      "source_hash": 4125305962161372538,
      "context_hash": 10802058845677411538,
      "translation": "\"agent\"는 \"independent continuant\"의 하위 클래스",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "Continuant": "Continuant"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:29:10.798095Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:60/seg:0",
      "source": "\"independent continuant\" subclass of \"continuant\"",
      "source_hash": 12656862110417148553,
      "context_hash": 16024680689473178475,
      "translation": "\"independent continuant\"는 \"continuant\"의 하위 클래스",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "Continuant": "Continuant"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:29:10.798095Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:61/seg:0",
      "source": "\"continuant\" subclass of \"entity\"",
      "source_hash": 15146869566976229603,
      "context_hash": 10032440458173183461,
      "translation": "\"continuant\"는 \"entity\"의 하위 클래스",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "Continuant": "Continuant"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:29:10.798095Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:62/seg:0",
      "source": "\"entity\" instance of \"class\"",
      "source_hash": 3904573287599417654,
      "context_hash": 15368218735533165593,
      "translation": "\"entity\"는 \"class\"의 인스턴스",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:29:10.798095Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:63/seg:0",
      "source": "With that you can categorize everything.",
      "source_hash": 14681003243454994759,
      "context_hash": 11428656319484724112,
      "translation": "이것으로 모든 것을 분류할 수 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:29:10.798095Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:63/seg:1",
      "source": "Well, almost everything—as Hamlet might, \"There are more things in Heaven and Earth than are dreamt of in your ontology.\" But BFO comes impressively close.",
      "source_hash": 16739793402881579155,
      "context_hash": 2421653966697283586,
      "translation": "물론 거의 모든 것입니다. 햄릿이라면 \"하늘과 땅에는 자네의 온톨로지로는 꿈도 꾸지 못할 것들이 있다네.\"라고 말했을 것입니다. 하지만 BFO는 놀라울 만큼 그에 가깝습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-10-17T13:29:10.798095Z",
      "issues": []
    }
  ]
}